    {
      "CVE": "CVE-2026-107778",
      "Description": "MIT Kerberos 5 (krb5) through 1.22.2 contains a NULL pointer dereference in make_cred_list() in rd_cred.c that allows authenticated Kerberos clients to crash services by sending mismatched KRB-CRED arrays. Attackers can send forwarded credentials with more tickets than ticket_info entries through gss_accept_sec_context() to crash GSS-API acceptor services, causing denial of service.",
      "Threats": [
        {
          "Type": "Impact",
          "Severity": "moderate"
        }
